{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB extension cables fit how I use readers, adapters, and computer peripherals: making connections easier to reach would improve equipment I already use.",
    "The Echo Dot with a clock and smart plug fits my Alexa setup while adding useful functions for another room, which gives me a reason to choose it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV devices and Echo Show 8 fit my interests, but my recent Fire TV Stick 4K Max and Show 5 stand make those purchases feel unnecessary right now.",
    "The compact keyboard supports Bluetooth, but I recently chose a full-size keyboard with a numeric keypad and would miss that functionality.",
    "The DisplayPort cable and amplifier solve needs I have not expressed, and the AirTag assumes access to an iPhone that my history does not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated Alexa and Fire TV purchases seem to be treated as reasons to buy more similar devices, even when my current equipment already covers their main purpose.",
    "My computer accessory purchases seem to be taken as interest in broadly related electronics, although I choose accessories for specific connections and practical needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Recent purchases matter: a new keyboard, streaming device, and display stand suggest I am still using those setups rather than looking to replace them.",
    "I am more interested in an accessory that makes existing equipment easier to use, or a device that adds a useful function, than another product with the same purpose.",
    "My past memory-card use makes expanded storage relevant, but it does not mean I currently need more capacity."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my Alexa and computer accessory interests, but often miss whether an item adds useful functionality or duplicates something I recently bought."
}"}
